<title>INDIA: India's SEBI clears 14 fixed-income schemes.</title>
<headline>India's SEBI clears 14 fixed-income schemes.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Market regulator the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) said on Thursday it has approved 14 fixed-income securities' schemes which plan to invest primarily in the debt market.</p>
<p>&quot;We have cleared 14 schemes which are likely to invest largely in the debt market,&quot; said Pratip Kar, SEBI executive director.</p>
<p>Kar said schemes by Alliance Capital, Templeton, Birla Global and Tata-Kleinwort Benson were among those cleared.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
